<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil firm, meal down a tad.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil firm, meal down a tad.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were firm on limited arrivals in markets against good demand from processing plants. Prices were up by 100-150 rupees per tonne. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also firm on limited supply from plants against better demand in local market. Soyoil solvent was up by 300 rupees and soyoil refined was up by 400 rupees per tonne. The undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly down on limited export demand. Soymeal yellow was $268-270 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $123-124 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,250 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,200-4,225 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
